From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 01:40:10 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 35/79] compute lane: a ChatML turn close after the held EOS
 goes in with the result turn

Qwen templates (Qwen3.x, Qwen3.8-Flash-Next) close every turn with
<|im_end|> and a newline. The lane rendered the call turn, saw its last
token was the newline rather than an EOS, logged "this template's
tool-result turn does not extend the call turn" and ended the reply at
the call: on Flash-Next every lane call came back empty with
finish=length.

The call turn now ends at its last EOS when only the template's
whitespace follows it; that close is the template's, not the model's,
so it is forced in with the result turn. The history must still stand
unchanged under the results, and a call turn with no EOS of its own
still ends the reply.

The new test drives the chat route with a Qwen template: on the old
code the held call gets one empty resume; now the result turn goes in
from the newline on and the reply goes on to its answer.
